.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-capture - Capture a payment (prepare, sign, and broadcast)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments capture  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prepare the transaction that calls capture() on the RAIL0 contract.

.PP
The payment must be in 'authorized' or 'partially_captured' status.
Partial captures are supported: pass --amount less than capturableAmount
to capture a portion; the remaining balance stays available until
authorizationExpiry. Note that capturableAmount is the LAST CONFIRMED balance,
so it is stale while another capture of yours is still in flight — 'payments
wait' settles it before you choose an amount.
The API returns 202 immediately. The payment stays at "authorized" until
rail0-indexer confirms and the API transitions it to "captured" or
"partially_captured". Poll 'payments get \&' until the payment
reaches the expected state and the capture transaction shows confirmed.

.PP
Pass --private-key (-p): the CLI signs locally and broadcasts in one step.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--amount\fP=""
	Amount to capture as a decimal in token units (e.g. 1.00); > 0 and ≤ the last confirmed capturable

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for capture

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=""
	Caller's secp256k1 private key (0x-prefixed hex); signs and broadcasts in one step

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	Max time to wait when --wait is set

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until the operation confirms on-chain (or fails)

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Full capture
  rail0 payments capture 0xrail0Id… --amount 1.00 -p 0xPayeeKey…

  # Partial capture
  rail0 payments capture 0xrail0Id… --amount 0.50 -p 0xPayeeKey…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
